				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\:W=100\times\:\:\frac{{T}_{0}-{T}_{t}}{{T}_{0}}$$\end{document}

The Tg of the coating polymers scraped off the glass substrate was measured using the differential scanning calorimetry (DSC) technique on a DSC Q2000 instrument (TA Instruments, USA) at a heating rate of 10 °C/min from −40 to 100 °C. The pendulum hardness of the coatings was evaluated according to CSN EN ISO 1552 using a Persoz-type pendulum TQC SP0500 (TQC Sheen, The Netherlands). The pendulum hardness of coatings was measured by the count of the pendulum oscillations with an electronic counter. First, the oscillation counts of the pendulum on the glass plate (reference) were adjusted to 423 ± 3 when the pendulum’s amplitude decreased from 12 to 4°. Then the oscillation counts of the pendulum on coatings with glass plate as the substrate were measured and recorded as n. The relative pendulum hardness H (%) was calculated using Eq. (2):2\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym}
